  "question": {
    "text": "A power transmission line feeds input power at<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> to a step-down transformer with its primary windings having <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo></math>turns giving the output power at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>230</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>. If the current in the primary coil of the transformer is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and its efficiency is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>90</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>%</mi></math>, the output current would be:"
  },
